WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.460
It's Monday, and this is the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.270
Here are the last 24 hours at Microsoft, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.140
Save the date. In Teams meetings,

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:21.150
two presenters sharing screens at once is now due in January.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.430
Handy for co-teaching or student pairs. It was due in December.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.400
Teachers,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:38.410
here's one for families: Minecraft's new Parents' Guide explains child accounts and parental controls.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.890
Child accounts start with online play and chat switched off,

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.590
and the Peaceful setting keeps creepers away.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.750
It even explains Minecraft Education, with its lesson library,

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.440
in-game coding and accessibility features.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:57.740
For students who zoom in, Windows' Magnifier gets a help menu,

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.600
for Release Preview Insiders.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.210
For student coders,

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:05.740
VS Code's new Inbox mode puts the agent sessions that need you on top.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.450
Press Windows + R? The new Run box opens in 94 milliseconds, in Release Preview.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.320
Streaming school events from Teams?

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:20.960
A switchboard for NDI video sources is due this month.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.690
Campus IT? Microsoft Ignite runs November 17 to 20,

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.570
with every breakout streamed live.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.820
In the lab,

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:37.280
Microsoft researchers hid 90 poisoned examples in 9,000 agent conversations, about 1%.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.000
Then a routine request made the agent run an attacker's command,

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.610
about 78% of the time.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.660
The fine print? VS Code drops its Local agent harness in February,

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.920
so move to the Copilot harness.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.630
And due February: opt-in face recognition in Teams Rooms.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.730
School IT can switch it off.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.730
After hours,

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:07.680
Minecraft's first drop of 2027 adds a Throwing Disc that comes back.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.980
Craft it in copper, iron, gold, diamond or netherite,

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:15.770
and Bedrock players get a full off-hand.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:23.550
And Xbox's 25th anniversary magazine is now online. Fable fans: page 38.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.240
Busy calendar? Pencil in what matters to your class, and save the date.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.350
Zoom out, and it never stops shipping.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.340
Today's board: shipped. Tomorrow's: already building.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
That's one day of updates. Imagine a whole year.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.870
You've been watching the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?
